      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Network trafficking is by nature not a solid one file at a time transfer when it comes to the internet.\nThey get sent in packages piece by piece so that if one is lost in transit it can be re-requested, and if you got a really lousy connection then forcing traffic to re-request the same package will stall the process and delay the total transfer.\nSo paralell tasking is the smoothest option as if you force one at a time then the one you wana see first might be forced to come last.\nI would agree tho that prioritizing small files first is a great idea that i was about to propose my self.\nAs it would encourage avatar makers to make their avatars smaller instead of larger downloads.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
