      "value": "@{5fafbc5d0241416661e39ee1|full_name}: This doesn't quite work. Parallel downloads on a slow connection very quickly have a detrimental effect as each download thread becomes starved and starts to struggle, in turn resulting in it taking *longer* to download everything, the opposite of the desired effect.\nParallel downloads can work on slow connections, but it needs to be a very small number (how much depends on the connection itself, but as low as 2 would be enough on a slow connection to avoid any \"unused\" bandwidth periods). Parallel downloads on a slow connection also cause the voice chat to become bandwidth starved too and break up badly.\nI have these issues on an 18Mb connection, so I hate to think what anyone on a slower line experiences.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
